e", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01E62fdbY1NGFeuhWaPqqCxJ", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 54186, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01E62fdbY1NGFeuhWaPqqCxJ", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 55351, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_019taVDrZuPwsbNvVzWBNz3S", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 55651, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_019taVDrZuPwsbNvVzWBNz3S", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 55651, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_019taVDrZuPwsbNvVzWBNz3S", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 60287, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened SEV2 incident INC-0001.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. Before the rollback, every region was on v2.3.1, the service was failing health checks and the error rate was about 18%. The release candidate for v2.3.1 had also been marked unhealthy.\n- **What went wrong along the way:** The first rollback attempt stopped with an orchestrator error after updating only us-east, leaving the regions on different versions. Retrying the same rollback was safe, so I ran it again and it finished us-west and eu-west. All regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) now run v2.3.0, and the error rate is about 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** The request to create the incident timed out, but the incident list shows it was created. I didn't resend it, so there's only one incident and one page went out. Its summary covers the failing v2.3.1 release and the rollback, including the retry. It also lists two follow-ups: find why v2.3.1 failed and why the orchestrator stopped the first rollback.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01H9fTPL91tha6v4U8P67bkc", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01DK288UxeAaQsgaQ7D9CfMs", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_0133KpyzY6eQ2qDHwDrmVhPQ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01PQT3dAswwisAWgigj18gM5", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback only finished in us-east. Rolling back to the same version again is safe to repeat, so I'll retry once to finish the other regions.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01ThhLUhpfjLKmkhn717a5cM", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01B1AR5vdonKWGwzJhm8aFMQ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01BHNwZaB57JLmmznroGwpz3", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01E62fdbY1NGFeuhWaPqqCxJ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 (latest deploy) was failing health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an error rate of about 18%. The v2.3.1-rc build had also been marked unhealthy. I rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release. The first rollback attempt failed partway with an orchestrator error after us-east, which left the regions on mixed versions. A second attempt completed in us-west and eu-west. All regions now run v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is about 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure and the orchestrator error that stopped the rollout.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_019taVDrZuPwsbNvVzWBNz3S", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened SEV2 incident INC-0001.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. Before the rollback, every region was on v2.3.1, the service was failing health checks and the error rate was about 18%. The release candidate for v2.3.1 had also been marked unhealthy.\n- **What went wrong along the way:** The first rollback attempt stopped with an orchestrator error after updating only us-east, leaving the regions on different versions. Retrying the same rollback was safe, so I ran it again and it finished us-west and eu-west. All regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) now run v2.3.0, and the error rate is about 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** The request to create the incident timed out, but the incident list shows it was created. I didn't resend it, so there's only one incident and one page went out. Its summary covers the failing v2.3.1 release and the rollback, including the retry. It also lists two follow-ups: find why v2.3.1 failed and why the orchestrator stopped the first rollback.", "type": "text"}]}]}